ttyrec is to roguelike as mpeg is to movie. Except it's a bit more
compact.

The first several links found by

   http://www.google.com/search?q=ttyrec+nethack

should answer most of your questions.

If you play on NAO, then ttyrecs of every game you play are saved
automatically. If you play on Windows or Linux, then the ttyrec
program can record your session, character by character. I'm not
sure what other platforms it works on.

ttyplay plays them back, in real time or accelerated.




